For the analysis of the probability of success, as-
sume that there is no time-out, that is, the algorithm
runs long enough to find the minimum. We refer to
this as the infinite algorithm. We start by analyzing
the expected time to find the minimum.
At any moment the infinite algorithm searches the
minimum among the t items which are less than T[y].
During the execution any such element will be chosen
at some point as the threshold with some probabil-
ity. The following lemma states that this probability
is the inverse of the rank of the element and is inde-
pendent of the size of the table.
